{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>If the sun has risen upon him.</b> That he came out from the tunnel into the air of the world, to the place of the sun's shining." "<b>He has blood-guilt.</b> The thief has against the one who kills him a claim of payment for bloodshed, since he was not found holding him inside the tunnel itself — for he was permitted to kill him only at the time of the heat of the crime, as in the case of tunneling." "<b>He shall surely make restitution.</b> Payment of fourfold and fivefold."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:40.728611404Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}